eld-2}}+{c}_{2}{e}^{-2t}\\begin{bmatrix}t \\\\ -t+1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe line that passes through the origin and is parallel to $$\n\\displaystyle v=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$ has the equation \n\n$$\ny={{field-3}}\n$$\n\nand the straight-line solutions of the form\n$$\n\\displaystyle {c}_{1}{e}^{-2t}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nlie on that line. \n\nSince ${e}^{-2t}\\to $ \n{{field-4}} \nas $t\\to \\infty ,$ these solutions approach \n{{field-5}}  \nas $t\\to \\infty .$\n\nLet's add the solutions to the phase space.\n\n![](images/45/4522e4e6ed382e821aaa47d40a191135161f95eef276b6e8ba3a8514e6bfdfd8.png)\n\nNow, consider solutions of the form\n$$\n\\displaystyle {c}_{2}{e}^{-2t}\\begin{bmatrix}t \\\\ -t+1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\nWhen ${c}_{2}=1,$ we get the following curve:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x={{field-6}} \\\\ y=(-t+1){e}^{-2t}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nComputing the coordinates (rounded to two decimal places) of several points on the curve, we get the table below.\n\n| $t$ | $-0.5$ | $0$ | $0.5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | {{field-7}} | $0$ | $0.18$ |\n| $y$ | {{field-8}} | $1$ | $0.18$ |\n\nLet's add the solutions to the phase space.\n\n![](images/db/dbf5a13ecd5e81c399204fd29d235e410fcb62274555cf3e5b32a383c1078d24.png)\n\nThe phase portrait of our system looks as follows:\n\n![](images/a6/a680b8c9319290df3beb20d7db964f385b368b01ead33961e2c10d22b19db4eb.png)"] [17592186545820 "Find $\\text{rank}(A)$ given that $$\n\\displaystyle \\text{Null}(A)=\\left\\{\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ 0 \\\\ {x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\right.\\,|\\,\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R\\}.\n$$"]}
